<p>Hi <%= @user.name %>,</p>

<p>
  <%= @whodunnit.name %> <%= "(an #{@is_manager ? "organization manager" : "HCB admin"})" unless @whodunnit == User.system_user %> has turned on a two-factor authentication requirement for <%= @event.name %>.
  From now on, every member of <%= @event.name %> needs two-factor authentication enabled on their HCB account.
</p>

<% if @already_enabled %>
  <p>
    You already have two-factor authentication enabled, so there's nothing you need to do. Thanks for keeping your account secure!
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    <strong>You don't have two-factor authentication enabled yet.</strong>
    <% if @deadline.present? %>
      Please <%= link_to "enable it in your security settings", settings_security_url %> by <strong><%= @deadline.strftime("%B #{@deadline.day.ordinalize}") %></strong>.
      After that, you'll lose access to <%= @event.name %> until you turn it on.
    <% else %>
      Please <%= link_to "enable it in your security settings", settings_security_url %> as soon as you can, or you'll lose access to <%= @event.name %>.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <p>
    To get set up, verify your phone number and turn on two-factor authentication under "Login preferences". You can also add an authenticator app or a security key on the same page.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  From,<br>
  The HCB Team
</p>
